# build artifacts -- currently untracked and easy to commit by accident
*.o
*.mod
lhbiem

# Figures ARE tracked, both png and pdf -- hbi_analysis/refresh_figures.sbatch
# regenerates them, but having them in the repo means they can be viewed without
# a Sherlock account. Note png does not delta-compress: each regenerate-and-commit
# adds a fresh full-size blob permanently, so avoid committing every refresh --
# commit when a figure's content actually changes.

# The Cooper Basin analysis. origin is a PUBLIC fork -- docs/ was pushed there
# by mistake and purged from all four affected branches on 2026-09-19. It is
# version-controlled ONLY in the private repo (docs-private / cooper-docs), and
# is synced there with `bash docs/sync_private.sh`. Keep it ignored so it can
# never be committed to the fork again.
docs/
